== Aftermath ==
The victory meant that Argentina had knocked the Netherlands out in both of the latter's two most recent World Cup appearances. Argentina advanced to the semi-finals to face [[Croatia national football team|Croatia]], who had prevailed in their quarter-final against [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]], also on penalties.<ref name="Makinde2022">{{cite web |last=Makinde |first=Tosin |title=Unserious World Cup: The most ridiculous performances from the quarterfinals and semifinals |url=https://www.cbssports.com/soccer/news/unserious-world-cup-the-most-ridiculous-performances-from-the-quarterfinal-and-semifinal/|access-date=25 January 2023 |website=CBSSports|date=17 December 2022 |archive-date=25 January 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230125041758/https://www.cbssports.com/soccer/news/unserious-world-cup-the-most-ridiculous-performances-from-the-quarterfinal-and-semifinal/|url-status=live}}</ref> However, the team would be without full-backs Marcos Acuña and Gonzalo Montiel, who would have to miss the next round due to yellow card accumulation throughout the tournament.<ref name=Booth2022 />

Argentina players were seen gloating to the Netherlands side immediately after Lautaro Martínez scored the winning penalty, with defender [[Nicolás Otamendi]] mimicking Messi's earlier gesture by cupping his hands around his ears while running in front of the Dutch players.<ref name=Douglas2022 /> Otamendi would explain that their reaction was in retaliation to the Netherlands players trying intimidation tactics during the penalty shoot-out.<ref name=Lambourne2022 /><ref name="Damms2022">{{cite web |last=Damms |first=Colin M. |url=https://www.sbnation.com/2022/12/10/23502579/argentinas-shootout-win-classic |title=Argentina's shootout win over Netherlands was World Cup perfection |work=[[SB Nation]] |date=10 December 2022 |accessdate=20 December 2022|archive-date=18 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221218213355/https://www.sbnation.com/2022/12/10/23502579/argentinas-shootout-win-classic|url-status=live}}</ref> Several Dutch players responded to the Argentine celebrations by engaging in another physical altercation, where the referee [[Fouls and misconduct (association football)#Red card (dismissal)|sent off]] Dumfries for a second yellow card.<ref>{{cite web |last=Meyers |first=Billy |title=How did Dumfries Get a Red Card Against Argentina? £12m Arsenal Target in Netherlands Chaos |url=https://www.hitc.com/en-gb/2022/12/10/how-did-dumfries-get-a-red-card-against-argentina-12m-arsenal-target-in-netherlands-chaos/ |website=[[HITC]] |date=10 December 2022 |accessdate=12 July 2023 |archive-date=21 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221221212430/https://www.hitc.com/en-gb/2022/12/10/how-did-dumfries-get-a-red-card-against-argentina-12m-arsenal-target-in-netherlands-chaos/ |url-status=live}}</ref> Messi exchanged heated words with Netherlands manager Louis van Gaal after the final whistle. As Emiliano Martínez left the pitch, he shouted obscenities towards Van Gaal and the Netherlands bench.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Swan |first=Rob |url=https://www.givemesport.com/88093337-world-cup-emi-martinez-lost-it-with-louis-van-gaal-after-argentina-beat-netherlands/ |title=World Cup: Emi Martinez lost it with Louis van Gaal after Argentina beat Netherlands |publisher=GiveMeSport |date=10 December 2022 |accessdate=10 July 2023 |archive-date=18 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221218225720/https://www.givemesport.com/88093337-world-cup-emi-martinez-lost-it-with-louis-van-gaal-after-argentina-beat-netherlands |url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Post-match comments ===
''The Telegraph'' wrote that the post-match interviews continued the "aggressive" nature of the game, with Messi snapping at the Dutch camp as he talked.<ref name=Burt2022 /> One incident saw Messi say {{lang|es|"¿Qué mirás, bobo? ¿Qué mirás, bobo? Andá pa' allá, bobo, andá pa' allá"}} roughly translating to "What are you looking at, fool? What are you looking at, fool? Go away, fool, go away" toward Weghorst.<ref>{{cite web |last=Codocea |first=Mauricio |url=https://www.sportingnews.com/es/futbol/news/que-miras-bobo-messi-declaraciones/cbgypvo3otjma4tewsgs5gqi |title="¿Qué mirás, bobo?": Lionel Messi enojado y unas declaraciones para la historia tras vencer a Países Bajos |work=[[Sporting News]] |date=9 December 2022 |accessdate=27 December 2022 |language=Spanish|archive-date=28 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221228032819/https://www.sportingnews.com/es/futbol/news/que-miras-bobo-messi-declaraciones/cbgypvo3otjma4tewsgs5gqi|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Torrisi |first=Antonio |url=https://www.goal.com/it/notizie/weghorst-messi-volevo-mostrargli-il-mio-rispetto-ma-almeno-sa-il-mio-nome/blt5df32efba1a3eaef |title=Weghorst risponde a Messi: "Volevo mostrargli il mio rispetto, ma almeno sa il mio nome" |publisher=[[Goal (website)|GOAL]] |date=22 December 2022 |accessdate=27 December 2022 |language=Italian|archive-date=28 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221228032817/https://www.goal.com/it/notizie/weghorst-messi-volevo-mostrargli-il-mio-rispetto-ma-almeno-sa-il-mio-nome/blt5df32efba1a3eaef|url-status=live}}</ref> The moment drew buzz on social media, spawning many Internet memes.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.cronista.com/mundial-qatar-2022/que-mira-bobo-reaparecio-wout-weghorst-el-19-de-paises-bajos-y-explico-que-le-quiso-decir-a-lionel-messi/ |title="Qué mirá' bobo": reapareció Wout Weghorst, el 19 de Países Bajos, y explicó qué le quiso decir a Lionel Messi |work=[[El Cronista]] |date=12 December 2022 |accessdate=27 December 2022 |language=Spanish|archive-date=28 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221228032819/https://www.cronista.com/mundial-qatar-2022/que-mira-bobo-reaparecio-wout-weghorst-el-19-de-paises-bajos-y-explico-que-le-quiso-decir-a-lionel-messi/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Sawai2022">{{cite web |last=Sawai |first=Akshay |url=https://www.outlookindia.com/sports/fifa-world-cup-2022-lionel-messi-fulfils-destiny-with-penalties-once-his-weakness-news-246118 |title=FIFA World Cup 2022: Lionel Messi Fulfils Destiny With Penalties, Once His Weakness |work=[[Outlook (Indian magazine)|Outlook]] |date=19 December 2022 |accessdate=27 December 2022|archive-date=19 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221219083454/https://www.outlookindia.com/sports/fifa-world-cup-2022-lionel-messi-fulfils-destiny-with-penalties-once-his-weakness-news-246118|url-status=live}}</ref> Weghorst reportedly just wanted to shake Messi's hand, causing some media outlets to view Messi's comments toward him as verbally abusive or "unfair".<ref name=Douglas2022 /><ref name=Sawai2022 />

Messi would tell reporters after the match that he felt disrespected by Van Gaal's pre-match comments and stated, "some Dutch players spoke too much during the game".<ref name=ESPN2022 /> He further criticised the Netherlands' tactics in the second half, stating "Van Gaal says that they play good football, but what he did was put on tall people and hit long balls." Emiliano Martínez also said "I heard Van Gaal saying we've got an advantage in penalties, and if they go to penalties they win, I think he needs to keep his mouth shut."<ref name=Grounds2022 />

Despite his comments, Messi later expressed regret for his actions during and after the match. He called them a result of several moments of tension between the two sides.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.foxsports.com/stories/soccer/lionel-messi-dishes-on-world-cup-regrets-actions-in-netherlands-match |title=Lionel Messi Dishes On World Cup, Regrets Actions in Netherlands Match |work=[[Fox Sports]] |date=30 January 2023 |accessdate=20 February 2023|archive-date=20 February 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230220064102/https://www.foxsports.com/stories/soccer/lionel-messi-dishes-on-world-cup-regrets-actions-in-netherlands-match|url-status=live}}</ref> Van Gaal, who resigned from the Netherlands team after exiting the tournament, would reignite the war of words several months later by expressing his belief that the tournament was [[match fixing|premeditated]] for Argentina to win. However, Netherlands captain Virgil van Dijk distanced himself from Van Gaal's comments, and said that neither he nor the other Netherlands players stood behind their former manager in this regard.<ref>{{cite web |last=Davey |first=Lee |url=https://talksport.com/football/1556329/louis-van-gaal-world-cup-rigged-lionel-messi/ |title=Louis van Gaal makes shock claim that the 2022 World Cup was rigged to help Argentina and Lionel Messi win |website=[[Talksport]] |date=5 September 2023 |accessdate=5 September 2023 |archive-date=5 September 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230905173845/https://talksport.com/football/1556329/louis-van-gaal-world-cup-rigged-lionel-messi/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

== Reception ==
[[File:20191002 Fußball, Männer, UEFA Champions League, RB Leipzig - Olympique Lyonnais by Stepro StP 0043-2 (cropped).jpg|thumb|280x280px|Match referee [[Antonio Mateu Lahoz]] received heavy criticism for his performance.]]
The game was noted by many football writers to be dramatic and hotly contested, with some labeling it as an "instant classic."{{refn|Sources that share such an opinion include:<ref name=ESPN2022 /><ref name=Douglas2022 /><ref name=Burt2022 /><ref name=Damms2022 /><ref>{{cite web |last1=Sangal |first1=Aditi |last2=Meyer |first2=Matt |url=https://www.cnn.com/sport/live-news/world-cup-quarter-finals-12-09-2022/index.html |title=December 9, 2022 World Cup news and highlights |publisher=[[CNN]] |date=9 December 2022 |accessdate=20 December 2022|archive-date=19 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221219003201/https://www.cnn.com/sport/live-news/world-cup-quarter-finals-12-09-2022/index.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Chisnall |first1=Craig |last2=Brown |first2=Luke |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/3987289/2022/12/10/argentina-netherlands-world-cup/ |title=How Argentina vs Netherlands descended into chaos – taunts, tantrums and tears |work=[[The Athletic]] |date=10 December 2022 |access-date=10 December 2022|url-access=subscription|archive-date=18 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221218220130/https://theathletic.com/3987289/2022/12/10/argentina-netherlands-world-cup/|url-status=live}}</ref>|group=n|name=varsources}} Several fans and reports of the game would refer to the match as ''The Battle of Lusail''.{{refn|Sources that refer to the match as such include:<ref name=ESPN2022 /><ref name=Burt2022 /><ref>{{cite web |last=Furniss |first=Matt |url=https://theanalyst.com/eu/2022/12/netherlands-2-2-argentina-world-cup-stats/ |title=Netherlands 2-2 Argentina: The Battle of Lusail |work=[[The Analyst]] |date=9 December 2022 |accessdate=11 December 2022|archive-date=11 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221211152624/https://theanalyst.com/eu/2022/12/netherlands-2-2-argentina-world-cup-stats/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Storey |first=Daniel |url=https://talksport.com/football/1273190/denzel-dumfries-netherlands-argentina-world-cup/ |title=Lionel Messi moves a step closer to World Cup immortality after Argentina win the 'Battle of Lusail' |website=[[Talksport]] |date=9 December 2022 |accessdate=27 December 2022|archive-date=30 January 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230130040648/https://talksport.com/football/1273190/denzel-dumfries-netherlands-argentina-world-cup/|url-status=live}}</ref>|group=n}} Reporting on the game, Jason Burt of ''[[The Daily Telegraph|The Telegraph]]'' wrote, "it was feisty, downright dirty and with huge amounts of gamesmanship."<ref name=Burt2022 /> The publication's Tom Morgan also wrote about the heated nature of the game: "on a feisty night full of tantrums, Argentina kept launching toys out of their pram even as Lautaro Martínez thrashed in his winner to send them through 4–3 on penalties."<ref>{{cite web |last=Morgan |first=Tom |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-cup/2022/12/09/picture-shames-argentina-otamendi-takes-victory-celebrations/ |title=Angry Lionel Messi lashes out as victorious Argentina launch toys out of their pram |work=[[The Daily Telegraph#Website|Telegraph.co.uk]] |date=9 December 2022 |accessdate=27 December 2022|url-access=subscription|archive-date=28 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221228030442/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-cup/2022/12/09/picture-shames-argentina-otamendi-takes-victory-celebrations/|url-status=live}}</ref>

The performance of referee [[Antonio Mateu Lahoz]] received heavy criticism, as he issued eighteen yellow cards, a record for World Cup matches, in addition to the red card during the match. Mateu Lahoz also overlooked a potential handball by Messi, while the length of the injury time added was considered excessive by some media outlets.<ref name="McNulty2022">{{cite web |last=McNulty |first=Phil |date=10 December 2022 |title=World Cup 2022: Messi the master as Argentina beat Netherlands in chaotic Qatar classic |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/63925260 |accessdate=10 December 2022 |work=BBC Sport |archive-date=10 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221210001629/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/63925260 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Hamilton2022">{{cite web |title=Argentina secure semifinal place over Netherlands after one of the wildest wins of Qatar 2022 |url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/fifa-world-cup/story/4828971/argentina-secure-semifinal-place-after-wildest-win-in-qatar |website=ESPN |access-date=10 December 2022 |date=9 December 2022 |first=Tom |last=Hamilton |archive-date=9 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221209235449/https://www.espn.com/soccer/fifa-world-cup/story/4828971/argentina-secure-semifinal-place-after-wildest-win-in-qatar |url-status=live}}</ref> Fans, pundits, and media alike considered a yellow card to be too lenient for some incidents.<ref name=ESPNRecord2022 /><ref name="Smith2022">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/63920253 |title=World Cup 2022: Netherlands and Argentina descend into chaos as new yellow card record set |date=10 December 2022 |last=Smith |first=Emma |publisher=BBC News|access-date=10 December 2022|archive-date=3 January 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230103081654/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/63920253|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=McNulty2022 /> Criticism was also levied particularly at his decision to caution players while the penalty shoot-out was happening, after open-play had ended.<ref name=Hamilton2022 /> [[BBC Sport]]'s Emma Smith wrote in her match report that he "did not help matters, to be kind. To be unkind, he had an absolute shocker – brandishing his yellow card with abandon ratcheted up tensions considerably, and by the time he finally showed red to [[Denzel Dumfries|Dumfries]], he had long since lost all control."<ref name=Smith2022 />

Smith also noted various players' unimpressed reactions to the referee.<ref name=Smith2022 /> Messi would say that "[FIFA] can't put a referee who isn't up to the task for these instances," while [[Emiliano Martínez]] described Mateu Lahoz as "useless" and said "I thought we controlled the game really well, we went 2–0 up and the ref was giving everything for them. They get a good header, and then it turned upside down, the ref gave 10 minutes for no reason. He just wanted them to score, that was basically it, so hopefully we don't have that ref any more."<ref name=ESPN2022 /> Netherlands midfielder [[Frenkie de Jong]] called Mateu Lahoz "scandalous" and said "when regular playing time was over, the Argentina players all went to him and from then on he only whistled for Argentina. Jurrien Timber's shoe was kicked off, but then he whistled for a foul against us. Luuk [de Jong] just wins a normal header and he blows his whistle, they kick the ball into our dugout, he doesn't care. Messi takes the ball with his hand, just lets it go."<ref>{{cite web |last=McVitie |first=Peter |url=https://www.goal.com/en-us/news/scandalous-netherlands-de-jong-referee-quarter-final-argentina/bltada1a6c8f74cbbd2 |title='Scandalous!' - Netherlands star De Jong says referee 'lost his way' in quarter-final defeat to Argentina |publisher=[[Goal (website)|Goal]] |date=10 December 2022 |accessdate=26 August 2024|archive-date=24 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221224155214/https://www.goal.com/en-us/news/scandalous-netherlands-de-jong-referee-quarter-final-argentina/bltada1a6c8f74cbbd2|url-status=live}}</ref> [[CBS Sports]] reported that after the match, Mateu Lahoz had been sent home.<ref name=Makinde2022 />

The match was further marred by the death of US sportswriter [[Grant Wahl]] after he collapsed near the end of the match while watching in the press box.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.cnn.com/2022/12/09/football/grant-wahl-death-world-cup-qatar-intl-hnk/index.html |title=American journalist Grant Wahl dies at Qatar World Cup |last=Yeung |first=Jessie |website=CNN.com |date=9 December 2022|access-date=9 December 2022 |language=en|archive-date=10 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221210033558/https://www.cnn.com/2022/12/09/football/grant-wahl-death-world-cup-qatar-intl-hnk/index.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Lewis |first=Russell |title=Longtime soccer sportswriter Grant Wahl has died covering the World Cup in Qatar |work=NPR |date=9 December 2022 |url=https://www.npr.org/2022/12/09/1142054844/grant-wahl-soccer-writer-dies-qatar-world-cup |publisher=National Public Radio |access-date=10 December 2022 |archive-date=17 January 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230117083429/https://www.npr.org/2022/12/09/1142054844/grant-wahl-soccer-writer-dies-qatar-world-cup |url-status=live}}</ref>

